cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal research artifact, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation V2"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "2.0.0-research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 derivation of the complete free linearized Dirac equation from a
  declared reciprocal complex-Psi/complex-chi C19 lattice action. The formal
  chain derives the action variation, exact native vacuum, finite-lattice
  tangent, cubical Clifford root, four-component readout, mass, time and three
  transport terms, and density/current bridge with controlled lattice and
  timestep corrections. It contains no external or maintained prepared
  background and makes no nonlinear localized-electron claim.
